## 1. Use case

Detail: `00-caso-de-uso.md`.

| Decision | Value |
|---|---|
| Trigger | HTTP, inbound REST adapter |
| Side effects | 1 — `INSERT` into `users` |
| Transaction | opens at the use case, closes before the response |
| Repetition | the same email never creates a second user |
| Freshness | none — a create returns what it just wrote |

---

## 2. Domain model — implement first

Detail: `10-dominio.md` § 1-4.

| Decision | Value |
|---|---|
| Aggregate | `User` — identity `UserId` (UUID v7, generated in the domain) |
| Value objects | `UserId`, `Email` |
| Use case | port `CreateUserUseCase` + `CreateUserService` (hexagonal vocabulary) |
| Output ports | `UserRepository` — `save`, `existsByEmail` |
| Exceptions | `ConflictException` with `errorCode` `EMAIL_ALREADY_USED`; `ValidationException` |
| Events | none |

---

## 3. Persistence — implement after 2

Detail: `20-persistencia.md` § 1-5. Migration SQL — or, for a `document (MongoDB)` aggregate, the
collection's schema declaration: § 4 of that partial — the executor materializes it verbatim.

| Decision | Value |
|---|---|
| Storage family | relational — `00-caso-de-uso.md` § Storage |
| Table | `users`, one per aggregate root |
| Business key | `UNIQUE (email)` |
| Concurrency | `@Version` optimistic lock |
| Migration | `V3__create_users.sql` — `<N>` re-checked on disk at implementation |
| Shared tables | `idempotency_keys` — NEW (first creation `POST` of the project) |

